---
import Chapter from '../Chapter.astro';
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
import FigUseCase from '../figures/FigUseCase.astro';

const cases = [
  {
    tag: 'In the thesis',
    title: 'Machine-to-machine mTLS',
    text: 'A service of one domain admits a client certificate issued in another, at connection time. Discover works inside the handshake. It is the case the laboratory implements end to end.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Beyond',
    title: 'Long-term signature validation',
    text: 'A PAdES signature made years ago in another domain must be judged against the trust in force when it was signed, not today. It needs the graph as it was: part of the ongoing doctoral research.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Beyond',
    title: 'Coalition S/MIME',
    text: 'Participants join and leave during an exercise, and every arrival is a new cross-certificate. It is where Govern is exercised most often.',
  },
];
---

<Chapter id="use-cases" num="10" kicker="Use cases" title="Where a governed path matters.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      One scenario runs through the whole thesis. A client of domain A connects over mTLS to a
      service of domain B. B trusts only its own root, and its intermediate has cross-certified the
      intermediate of A. <strong>Inside the handshake, B has to decide whether an admissible path
      exists under its policy, and which one is best.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure num={10} caption="The use case of the thesis. Its variants (a key renewal, a revocation, a higher threshold) are all told on this same scenario.">
    <FigUseCase />
  </Figure>

  <div class="cases grid-3">
    {
      cases.map((c) => (
        <div class="rule-top">
          <p class="label">{c.tag}</p>
          <h3>{c.title}</h3>
          <p class="small">{c.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .cases {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .cases .label {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .cases .small {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
